def get_slide_data() -> dict:
    return {
        'title': 'Phase 1: Physics Baseline + PINN Refinement',
        'content': '\n# Phase 1: Establishing the Physics Baseline\n\nBefore any optimization samples run, we need a **reference point** — a single full SPARTA simulation at the baseline geometry to calibrate all subsequent comparisons.\n\n## Step 1: Baseline Geometry Generation\n\n```python\nsubprocess.run([\n    python_exec, "HIAD_GeometryEngine.py",\n    "--diameter", "3.0",\n    "--angle",    "60.0",\n    "--toroids",  "6",\n    "--nose",     "0.550",\n    "--output",   "HIAD_custom"\n])\n```\n\nOutputs: `HIAD_custom.surf` (2D axisymmetric surface for SPARTA), `.step`, `.stl`\n\n## Step 2: SPARTA DSMC Baseline Run\n\n`run_sparta_simulation()` is called with the baseline parameters:\n- Generates `CADDesign/in.hiad` (full SPARTA input script)\n- Launches SPARTA via Docker: `mpirun -np N spa -in in.hiad`\n- Streams output line-by-line, writes `surf.*.out` + `grid.*.out`\n\n**Baseline Physics Environment:**\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Velocity | 2700 m/s (Mach ~10) |\n| Number density ($n_{\\rho}$) | $3.5 \\times 10^{22}$ /m³ (52 km) |\n| $T_{\\infty}$ | 270 K |\n| $T_{\\text{wall}}$ | 1000 K |\n| fnum | $1.5 \\times 10^{20}$ |\n\n## Step 3: Result Extraction (`parse_sparta_results()`)\n\nAverages the **last 15 dump files** to reduce statistical noise:\n\n$$F_D = \\text{mean}\\left(\\sum_{\\text{elements}} f_x\\right) \\quad \\dot{q} = \\text{mean}\\left(\\max_{\\text{elements}} \\text{KE flux}\\right)$$\n\nReturns: `{\'drag\': N, \'heat\': W/m², \'shock_temp\': K}`\n\n## Phase 1.2: PINN Refinement (Optional, `pinn_accel=True`)\n\nA **Physics-Informed Neural Network** (`source/pinn_accelerator.py`) is trained on the baseline SPARTA data to fill spatial gaps:\n\n- **Architecture**: FNN $[2] + [128 \\times 5] + [5]$, `tanh` activation\n- **Inputs**: $(x, y)$ grid coordinates\n- **Outputs**: $(\\rho, u, v, T, p)$ — 5 flow fields\n- **PDE**: 2D axisymmetric compressible Navier-Stokes (Sutherland viscosity)\n- **Two-stage training**: Data pre-training → physics-regularized fine-tuning\n\n**PINN correction factors** (clamped to $[0.5, 2.0]$):\n\n$$C_D^{\\text{PINN}} = C_D^{\\text{DSMC}} \\times \\frac{p_{\\text{PINN,max}}}{p_{\\text{raw,max}}} \\qquad \\dot{q}^{\\text{PINN}} = \\dot{q}^{\\text{DSMC}} \\times \\frac{T_{\\text{PINN,max}}}{T_{\\text{raw,max}}}$$\n'
    }
